# Prompt pipeline verification (MCP)

Mirrored for Antigravity: [`.agents/rules/prompt-run-test.md`](../../.agents/rules/prompt-run-test.md). Spec: [`_/specs/inst.md`](../../_/specs/inst.md).

## Hard rule (verify)

When fixing **wrong chat results**, **tool not called**, **wrong blocks/UI**, **inst/compose/RAG**, or any **prompt-turn** bug:

1. Reproduce — **exact user phrase**, or `msg_get` / `trace_get` on failing `msg_id`.
2. Fix in the **right layer** (below) — not a one-off string in `prompt_turn.rs`.
3. **`prompt_compose`** while iterating; **`prompt_run`** before **fixed / ready to test**.

| MCP tool | Use |
|----------|-----|
| `prompt_compose` | `inst_ids`, `inst_block`, `selected_tools` — no LLM |
| `prompt_run` | Full turn: tool hop, `blocks_json`, `text`, `trace` |

`owner_iid`: **99000** app-like · **33000** seed regression. Only those two on `/v1/mcp/agent`.

## Where steering lives (do not hardcode)

| What | Where | Not here |
|------|--------|----------|
| **When** to call a tool, reply shape, exclusions | **`ai.inst`** — `phrases`, `inst` body, `include_tools`, `exclude_tools` | Rust system prompt strings, `prompt_turn` one-offs |
| **What** the tool does (API, params) | **`ToolDefinition`** — `description`, JSON schema | Duplicated paragraphs in inst (inst = *when/how*, tool desc = *what*) |
| **Discovery** (RAG / filter) | Tool `topics`, `always`, **`rag_phrases`** | Extra keywords only in inst unless steering |
| Baseline persona | **`inst.core.assistant`** (`trigger: always`) in DB | Removed `inst!` Rust macros |
| Topic inheritance | **`ai.topic.inst`** chain | Ad-hoc topic text in code |
| Bot voice | **`identity.meta_json.inst_base`** | Home assistant pipeline |

**Never add new steering in Rust/Dart for Home compose** except:

1. **Mechanical context** — time/location/memory merge, tool-round wrapup hints  
2. **Web tools only** — see **Excluded: web pipeline** below  

Everything else: **`inst.sql` + live `inst_put`**, tool metadata, **`compose_force_*_tool_call`** (not Rust phrase lists or `reply_rule` in tool JSON).

### Excluded: web pipeline (`web.search`, `web.visit`, `web.research`)

These tools are **exempt from the no-hardcode steering rule**. Shared Rust orchestration is intentional; do not move into `ai.inst` or delete when auditing hardcoded prompts.

| Rust (keep) | Role |
|-------------|------|
| `WEB_GROUNDED_REPLY_RULE` | Anti-placeholder when `compose_force_web_tool_call` |
| `user_wants_search` | Prefetch / defer pairing with `inst.web_search` and catalog |
| Pre-hop `web.search` / chained `web.visit` in `tool_loop.rs` | Grounding before LLM hop 1 |
| `pick_visit_url` | Visit target after search |
| `catalog_web_*` | Site catalog phases keyed off `inst.site.catalog.*` |

**Still use `ai.inst` for web:** `inst.web_search` (phrases, when to search, local city in query, `include_tools` / `exclude_tools`). Inst steers *intent*; Rust runs the *pipeline*.

**Never provider grounding:** `web-grounding-cluster-only.mdc` — no Gemini `googleSearch` / `groundingConfig` or OpenAI `web_search` tool type; cluster `web.search` only.

**All other tools** (presentation, consumption, expense, site.create, gsheet, device, …): no Rust phrase prefetch, no steering in tool result JSON — **`ai.inst`** + **`compose_force_*`** only.

**Inst enrich** — facts only, not steering.

## Fixing missing or wrong tools

Use **`prompt_compose`** on the failing phrase and read `inst_ids` + `selected_tools` + trace candidates (`fed`, `sim`).

| Symptom | Check first | Fix |
|---------|-------------|-----|
| **`inst_ids: []`** (no `inst.core.assistant`) | Inst cache empty / pod | `inst_list_for_turn` reload; rollout; boot `inst_cache_init` |
| Phrase should match, no `inst.*` | `phrases[]` substring, `kind`, `scope`, `topics[]` | Update row; **`inst_put` live** (git seed alone is not live) |
| Tool never in catalog | Tool `topics` / `always` vs `active_topics` | Tool def metadata; compose `compose_inject_force_tools` via **`include_tools`** |
| Tool in catalog, not **fed** | RAG rank, `rag_phrases`, `exclude_tools` | Extend `rag_phrases`; inst `include_tools`; drop rivals with `exclude_tools` |
| Tool **fed**, model skips hop 1 | Weak `inst` body | Inst + **`compose_force_*_tool_call`** (non-web only; web uses web pipeline above) |
| Wrong tool wins | Competing inst / general web force | `exclude_tools` on winning inst; priority |

Debug order: **infra** → **eligibility** → **inst** → **RAG** → **inst wording / force_***. For web misses, check **inst.web_search** *and* prefetch/defer in Rust — not inst-only.

New Home tool: **`ToolDefinition` + `inst.sql` + live `ai.inst` row**. Stable **`description`**; extra match language in **`rag_phrases`**.

## Assert on `prompt_run`

1. Expected tool **`fed: true`** in `trace_tool_filter`
2. Hop 1 **`tool/`** when UI/data comes from a tool (not prose-only)
3. **`blocks_json`** — e.g. `presentation.deck`, meal/expense blocks
4. **`text`** matches tool result (no false "no access" / empty-data)

## Do not skip

No **fixed** claim without at least **`prompt_compose`** on the failing phrase; **`prompt_run`** for tool-call and chat-result bugs.

MCP errors: `C35_MCP_AGENT_ENABLED=1`, `C35_MCP_AGENT_KEY` on server_ai; reload MCP.
